Add foreground grass/rocks in screen space at end of draw before HUD. Function:
```
function drawForeground(){
 const sway=Math.sin(timer*.7)*4;
 ctx.save();
 ctx.fillStyle='#081114';
 // left corner clump of grass silhouettes
 for(let i=0;i<14;i++){x=...; y=H-6; h=...; draw thin blades}
 // right
 ctx.restore();
}
```
But bottom area H-540*... game screen bottom; HUD at bottom 24 covers 500-540. Foreground grass up to H-40 might interfere visually with HUD? HUD is DOM over canvas with text; grass behind is fine. Keep height 60.

Maybe add a foreground frame of pine branches at top corners? The vignette already darkens.

Add low snowbank silhouette across bottom with jagged grass:
```
ctx.beginPath(); moveTo(0,H); for x... y=H-18 - sin...; ... fill '#0a1518'
```
and grass blades at corners. This creates depth.

Do at end of draw after drawSnow? Snow should fall in front of foreground? Snow inside world is behind; foreground snow would be nice. Keep.

Add function and call.

